    "description": "## Objective\n\nCreate two global picklist value sets used by Deal, Operator, and future objects. Market and Vertical are picklists in Phase 1 (not custom objects).\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\n* Create global value set WT_Market with starting values (verbatim from the current rates data): ON; ON-CAN; ROC; USA; NJ-USA; PA-USA; MI-USA; IL-USA; OH-USA; KS-USA; NC-USA; NY-USA; MI/NJ-USA; OH/KS-USA; NC/MA-USA; Sweeps\n* Create global value set WT_Vertical with values: Sportsbook; Casino; DFS; Sweepstakes; Social Casino\n* Both sets restricted (no free-text entries)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n* Both global value sets exist with the values above and are available to reference from custom fields\n\n## Testing Notes\n\nReference each set from a scratch field, then delete the scratch field.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nMarket custom object (kept as a documented graduation path if reporting later needs state-level rollups).\n\n## Open Questions\n\n* ON and ON-CAN both appear in the source data — same market? Merge before go-live if so.\n* 'Sweeps' appears as a geography value in the rates file but looks like a vertical — client to confirm what it denotes.\n* Link tracker data adds WV, AZ, CO and Canada-wide variants (CA, Canada excl. Ontario) — add these values now or as needed?\n* Add Poker to WT_Vertical? One Poker deal exists in the data. And does Fantasy map to DFS?\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n* Value API names match the source data exactly so the data load (POC-11) needs no mapping step.\n* Composite values (MI/NJ-USA, OH/KS-USA) cannot roll up to state level in reports — accepted trade-off for Phase 1.\n\n---\n\nEstimate: XS · \\~2h · Dependencies: None · Ticket POC-05 (approved 2026-07-04)",
